{
  "id": "queue-kanji-exemptions",
  "title": "cards.kanji_exemptions: which kanji a word requires and which fronts carry furigana, on (default) and off (ADR-042)",
  "covers": [
    "queue.kanji_exemptions_on",
    "queue.kanji_exemptions_off"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "Stand-ins from the fixture dictionary for the cases of ADR-042 (海老, 今日, 薔薇 and 林檎 are not in fixtures/dict): 寿司 (kanji form tagged ateji: word-level exempt, like 海老), 昨日 (both kanji jōyō, irregular reading, no tag: like 今日), 鱈 (no grade, no frequency rank, no tag: no learnable kanji, the rule 薔薇 was meant to show) and a note 鱈子 without a dictionary entry (子 learnable, 鱈 not: the mixed case of 林檎). Four deckless new cards in that order (...10, ...20, ...30, ...40); no kanji note exists; the key is absent (= on).",
    "Step 0 (on): 寿司 alone with front_furigana true (text front 寿司（すし）); 昨, 日, 昨日 with a plain front (kanji_parts: neither reading aligns, used_reading null); 鱈 alone with front_furigana true; 子, 鱈子 with a plain front and no card for 鱈. The fetch mints three kanji notes (昨, 日, 子). until_stop is 7.",
    "Step 1 switches cards.kanji_exemptions off (the shell mints settings.set as the device, the server as the server device).",
    "Step 2 (off): every kanji is required and no front has furigana: 寿, 司, 寿司; 昨, 日, 昨日; 鱈, 鱈 (the word); 子, 鱈子 (its 鱈 was taken by the word 鱈, drawn first). The fetch mints 寿, 司 and 鱈. until_stop is 10."
  ],
